Falsifies `pci::verification::a_bar_size_is_where_the_writable_bits_begin`.

The defect: `size_from_mask` keeps the lowest-set-bit size and drops the contiguity check. The
lowest set bit is the right size for every mask a well-formed device returns, so every fixture
still passes, but a mask with a hole above its lowest bit, or a 64-bit mask whose upper half reads
zero, is then sized as though its writable bits ran to the top.

Expected to fail: the boundary assertion, on any mask with a clear address bit above its lowest
set one.

diff --git a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
@@ -403,9 +403,6 @@ fn size_from_mask(mask: u64, decode_bits: u64) -> Result<u64, BarRefusal> {
         return Err(BarRefusal::NoWritableBits);
     }
     let size = mask.isolate_lowest_one();
-    if mask != decode_bits & !(size - 1) {
-        return Err(BarRefusal::MaskNotContiguous);
-    }
     Ok(size)
 }
 
